You are working in /tmp/sv-31549307050c480a9f6d07283c36e07f/ShipmentTracker — a Blazor Web App (.NET 11) with Auto interactivity (Server + WebAssembly) and Individual authentication. The solution has two projects:

- `ShipmentTracker/` (server project)
- `ShipmentTracker.Client/` (client/WASM project)

The template already has Identity configured with SQLite, EF Core, and the standard Blazor layout.

**Your task**: Build a shipment tracking system for a logistics company. Implement the following:

---

## 1. Shared Models (in a new `ShipmentTracker.Shared` class library project)

Create a shared project `ShipmentTracker.Shared` so both server and client can reference the same models.

File: `ShipmentTracker.Shared/ShipmentTracker.Shared.csproj`
```xml
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net11.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
```

File: `ShipmentTracker.Shared/ShipmentDto.cs`
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Shared;

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string? CustomerEmail { get; set; }
    public string? Notes { get; set; }
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

Add `ShipmentTracker.Shared` to the solution and reference it from both `ShipmentTracker` and `ShipmentTracker.Client` projects.

---

## 2. Data Model (server project)

File: `ShipmentTracker/Data/Shipment.cs`
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Shared;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string? CustomerEmail { get; set; }
    public string? Notes { get; set; }
}
```

Update `ApplicationDbContext` to add:
```csharp
public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();
```

---

## 3. Seed Data

In `Program.cs` on the server, after building the app but before `app.Run()`, add database seeding:

```csharp
using (var scope = app.Services.CreateScope())
{
    var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<ApplicationDbContext>();
    db.Database.Migrate();
    if (!db.Shipments.Any())
    {
        db.Shipments.AddRange(
            new Shipment { TrackingNumber = "TRK-1001", Origin = "New York, US", Destination = "London, UK", Status = ShipmentStatus.InTransit, ShippedDate = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-3), EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(4), CustomerEmail = "alice@example.com", Notes = "Fragile items" },
            new Shipment { TrackingNumber = "TRK-1002", Origin = "Tokyo, JP", Destination = "Sydney, AU", Status = ShipmentStatus.Delivered, ShippedDate = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-7), EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-1), CustomerEmail = "bob@example.com" },
            new Shipment { TrackingNumber = "TRK-1003", Origin = "Berlin, DE", Destination = "Paris, FR", Status = ShipmentStatus.Pending, ShippedDate = DateTime.UtcNow, EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(2), CustomerEmail = "carol@example.com" },
            new Shipment { TrackingNumber = "TRK-1004", Origin = "Shanghai, CN", Destination = "Los Angeles, US", Status = ShipmentStatus.OutForDelivery, ShippedDate = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-10), EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow, CustomerEmail = "dave@example.com" },
            new Shipment { TrackingNumber = "TRK-1005", Origin = "Mumbai, IN", Destination = "Dubai, AE", Status = ShipmentStatus.Delayed, ShippedDate = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-5), EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(3), CustomerEmail = "eve@example.com", Notes = "Customs hold" }
        );
        db.SaveChanges();
    }
}
```

Add the necessary `using ShipmentTracker.Data;` and `using ShipmentTracker.Shared;` at the top of Program.cs.

---

## 4. API Endpoints (server project)

Add minimal API endpoints in Program.cs (before `app.Run()`):

```csharp
// Shipment API endpoints
var shipments = app.MapGroup("/api/shipments").RequireAuthorization();

shipments.MapGet("/", async (ApplicationDbContext db) =>
{
    return await db.Shipments.Select(s => new ShipmentDto
    {
        Id = s.Id,
        TrackingNumber = s.TrackingNumber,
        Origin = s.Origin,
        Destination = s.Destination,
        Status = s.Status,
        ShippedDate = s.ShippedDate,
        EstimatedDelivery = s.EstimatedDelivery,
        CustomerEmail = s.CustomerEmail,
        Notes = s.Notes
    }).ToListAsync();
});

shipments.MapGet("/{id:int}", async (int id, ApplicationDbContext db) =>
{
    var s = await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);
    if (s is null) return Results.NotFound();
    return Results.Ok(new ShipmentDto
    {
        Id = s.Id,
        TrackingNumber = s.TrackingNumber,
        Origin = s.Origin,
        Destination = s.Destination,
        Status = s.Status,
        ShippedDate = s.ShippedDate,
        EstimatedDelivery = s.EstimatedDelivery,
        CustomerEmail = s.CustomerEmail,
        Notes = s.Notes
    });
});

shipments.MapGet("/track/{trackingNumber}", async (string trackingNumber, ApplicationDbContext db) =>
{
    var s = await db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(x => x.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);
    if (s is null) return Results.NotFound();
    return Results.Ok(new ShipmentDto
    {
        Id = s.Id,
        TrackingNumber = s.TrackingNumber,
        Origin = s.Origin,
        Destination = s.Destination,
        Status = s.Status,
        ShippedDate = s.ShippedDate,
        EstimatedDelivery = s.EstimatedDelivery,
        CustomerEmail = s.CustomerEmail,
        Notes = s.Notes
    });
});

shipments.MapPut("/{id:int}/status", async (int id, ShipmentStatusUpdate update, ApplicationDbContext db) =>
{
    var s = await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);
    if (s is null) return Results.NotFound();
    s.Status = update.Status;
    if (update.EstimatedDelivery.HasValue)
        s.EstimatedDelivery = update.EstimatedDelivery.Value;
    if (update.Notes is not null)
        s.Notes = update.Notes;
    await db.SaveChangesAsync();
    return Results.Ok();
});
```

Also add a DTO for the status update in the Shared project:

File: `ShipmentTracker.Shared/ShipmentStatusUpdate.cs`
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Shared;

public class ShipmentStatusUpdate
{
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string? Notes { get; set; }
}
```

---

## 5. Client-side Service

File: `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentService.cs`
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Shared;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentService(HttpClient http)
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>("/api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentAsync(int id)
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>($"/api/shipments/{id}");
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> TrackShipmentAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await http.GetAsync($"/api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }

    public async Task<bool> UpdateStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatusUpdate update)
    {
        var response = await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"/api/shipments/{id}/status", update);
        return response.IsSuccessStatusCode;
    }
}
```

Register HttpClient and the service in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs`:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddSingleton<AuthenticationStateProvider, PersistentAuthenticationStateProvider>();
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress) });
builder.Services.AddScoped<ShipmentService>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

Also register these same services on the SERVER side so server-prerendering works. In the server `Program.cs`, add:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri("http://localhost:5000") });
builder.Services.AddScoped<ShipmentService>();
```
(Add `using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;` at the top.)

Actually, for server-side rendering during prerender, it's better to use a service that hits the DB directly. But for simplicity and since Auto mode will quickly switch to WASM, let's register HttpClient on the server too. Place `builder.Services.AddHttpClient();` and the scoped registrations before `var app = builder.Build();`.

